## Why This Is Asked
Tests time-expanded 3-valued reasoning and propagation strategies under Kleene semantics. It also checks ability to craft a concrete witness and reason about propagation order across time.

## Key Concepts
- Kleene 3-valued logic; time-expanded CSP; forward propagation; A→B = ¬A ∨ B; monotone reasoning; time-dimension constraints; backtracking with preference for U.

## Code Example
```javascript
function imply(a,b){
  const notA = a==='T'?'F': a==='F'?'T':'U';
  const order = { 'F':0, 'U':1, 'T':2 };
  return order[notA] > order[b] ? notA : b;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How to scale to k time steps, or add stochastic uncertainty? 
- How would you handle non-monotone operators across time?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests 3-valued dataflow reasoning, fixpoint propagation, and translating logic into a workable algorithm.

## Key Concepts
- Kleene three-valued logic (T, F, U)
- Worklist/fixpoint propagation
- Dataflow dependency graphs
- Handling cycles and convergence

## Code Example
```javascript
// Kleene 3-valued logic
const T = true, F = false, U = 'U';
function not(x){ if (x===T) return F; if (x===F) return T; return U; }
function and(a,b){ if (a===F || b===F) return F; if (a===T && b===T) return T; return U; }
function or(a,b){ if (a===T || b===T) return T; if (a===F && b===F) return F; return U; }

// program: A = B AND C; D = NOT E; F = D OR A
let B = U, C = T, E = U;
let A = and(B, C);
let D = not(E);
let F = or(D, A);
```

